<p>UAE authorities said a fire broke out at the Fujairah Oil Industry Zone on Monday after a drone attack that originated from Iran, injuring three Indian citizens who were hospitalized with moderate injuries. The UAE Defence Ministry said it also intercepted three cruise missiles fired from Iran over its territorial waters, while a fourth fell into the sea. The attacks were the first reported Iranian missile and drone strikes on the UAE since an April 8 ceasefire between Washington and Tehran paused more than two months of fighting in the Gulf region. They followed President Trump&#x27;s launch of &quot;Project Freedom,&quot; an effort to help commercial vessels leave the Strait of Hormuz, where shipping had been disrupted. The New York Times reported that the strikes also coincided with reported clashes between American and Iranian vessels in the Strait of Hormuz. The UAE Foreign Ministry condemned the strikes as a violation of international law and said the country reserved the right to respond. Iran did not immediately comment on the UAE accusations, while Iranian state media cited a senior military official as saying Tehran had no plan to target the UAE.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/uwlgNptEl7umu3DmOgCzQf57h8bCvJbgW_y9TyLJpetureMA6w8426w0evUbvIGTCStDlZ_1AaIHZg5TZCPG8RcMSlqflGISgxruQ3FDQK2J06Vx7tfN1fYwfWuH8fMYYgBiRy-bj8Wbi3d9c07SBGW7Apk4sDc6ZzkXthbxqr4magYVvox9b_3RPc2GoZ0Z' alt='Ships in the Strait of Hormuz, where commercial vessels have been stranded during the Gulf fighting.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Expanded tally: The National, citing the UAE Ministry of Defence, reported that air defences engaged 12 ballistic missiles, three cruise missiles and four drones launched from Iran on Monday.</li><li>Public alerts: Authorities sent mobile warnings in Dubai and Abu Dhabi about possible missile attacks and urged residents to follow official safety instructions.</li><li>Iranian map: Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guards Navy issued a map claiming expanded control near the Strait of Hormuz, including the UAE ports of Fujairah and Khorfakkan and the coast of Umm Al Quwain.</li><li>Emergency response: Fujairah Civil Defence teams deployed immediately and continued efforts to bring the fire under control.</li></ul><blockquote>We stand in solidarity with the UAE and will continue to support the defence of our partners in the Gulf. This escalation must cease. Iran needs to engage meaningfully in negotiations to ensure the ceasefire in the Middle East endures, and a long-term diplomatic solution is achieved - Keir Starmer</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Arab Emirates: The Foreign Ministry said the UAE would not compromise on protecting its security and sovereignty and held Iran fully responsible for the attacks and their repercussions. (<a href='https://thepeninsulaqatar.com/article/04/05/2026/uae-condemns-renewed-iranian-aggression-using-missiles-and-drones'>The Peninsula Qatar</a>)</li><li>Iran: Iranian officials warned U.S. naval forces to stay clear of Hormuz after Trump said Washington would help commercial vessels in the strait, The Express Tribune reported. (<a href='https://tribune.com.pk/story/2606277/iran-warns-us-navy-to-stay-clear-of-hormuz-after-trump-says-us-to-help-stranded-ships'>The Express Tribune</a>)</li><li>United States: President Trump warned Iran that it would face a strong military response if Iranian naval forces attacked U.S. forces escorting commercial vessels through the Strait of Hormuz. (<a href='https://www.thenews.com.pk/latest/1401378-trump-warns-iran-over-attack-on-navy-in-the-hormuz'>The News International</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-iran-war-ceasefire-donald-trump-hormuz-project-freedom-live-updates-ceasefire-on-brink-as-us-iran-trade-fire-uae-reports-attacks-11450031#publisher=newsstand'>US-Iran Ceasefire Live Updates: &quot;Stop Holding World Hostage,&quot; Germany Tells Iran After UAE Attacked</a> - ndtv.com